# Technical Investigation Report: Floating Action Pills, OSD Controls & Modal Dialogs (Milestone UI-M3)

- **Author**: Explorer 2 (`explorer_ui_m3_2`)
- **Role**: Floating Action Pills & OSD Controls Explorer
- **Milestone**: UI-M3 (Modernized Media Player HUD Overlay)
- **Target Platform**: LG 32LR686BPSA (1920x1080 Full HD, webOS 8.5.0, Chromium ~108+ WAM)
- **Reference Project**: `.tmp_ref/theboringtv-lgwebos/` (`style.css`, `features/details.css`)
- **Status**: COMPLETE & VERIFIED

---

## 1. Executive Summary

This report delivers the comprehensive architectural design and technical specification for modernizing the media player on-screen display (OSD) controls and modal dialogs in the CineJoy LG webOS application (`com.cinejoy.tv`). 

Specifically, this investigation covers:
1. **Floating Action Pill Buttons**: Transforming the playback controls (`#osd-play-btn`, `#osd-rewind-btn`, `#osd-forward-btn`, `#player-back-btn`) and auxiliary action pills (`#osd-subtitles-btn`, `#osd-server-btn`) into Google TV cinema-grade floating pills (`.pill`, `.osd-btn`, `.osd-pill-btn`).
2. **High-Contrast 10-Foot TV Spatial Focus States**: Engineering focus states with `scale(1.08)` to `scale(1.10)` elevation, dual-ring halos (`0 0 0 5px #FFFFFF` + `0 0 28px rgba(149, 255, 80, 0.65)` glow), and inverted color dynamics (`#e8eaed` white surface, `#202124` dark icon/text) visible from 10 feet away.
3. **Modal Dialog Modernization & Focus Trapping**: Designing the Subtitle and Audio/Server selection modals with Google TV sheet surfaces (`#202124`, `border-radius: 32px`), full-bleed backdrop scrims (`#0e1014`, blur), strict spatial focus trapping (`SpatialNav.trap`), and clean focus restoration to trigger elements.
4. **Elimination of All DOM Sinks**: Eradicating all 6 instances of `innerHTML` in `app/js/player.js` (lines 1650, 1657, 1693, 1695, 1736/1745, 1782/1796) by transitioning to pure DOM APIs (`document.createElement`, `document.createElementNS`, `textContent`, `setAttribute`, `appendChild`).
5. **Zero-Regression Invariant Preservation**: Retaining all 38 player DOM IDs, spatial navigation contracts (`data-nav-group`, `data-nav-tier`), and passing 100% of the 773 automated checks across 24 test suites.

---

## 2. Current Baseline & Invariant Analysis

### 2.1 DOM Structure & Element Inventory
In `app/index.html` (lines 1029–1250), the video player view (`#view-player`) contains 38 invariant DOM elements across 7 structural tiers:

| Tier | DOM ID | Tag / Classes | Spatial Nav Attributes | Purpose |
|------|--------|---------------|------------------------|---------|
| **Video Canvas** | `#main-video-player` | `<video class="player-video">` | None | HTML5 native video element |
| **Buffering** | `#player-buffering` | `<div class="player-buffering-overlay">` | `aria-live="polite"` | Centered loading spinner |
| | `#player-buffering-text` | `<span class="buffering-text">` | None | Stream connection status label |
| **Error Dialog** | `#player-error-dialog` | `<div class="player-modal-backdrop">` | `role="dialog" aria-modal="true"` | Fatal stream recovery backdrop |
| | `#player-error-title` | `<h2 class="player-modal-title">` | None | Error title |
| | `#player-error-message` | `<p class="player-modal-desc">` | None | Error description |
| | `#player-error-retry-btn` | `<button class="btn btn-primary">` | `data-nav="true" data-nav-group="player-error"` | Retry stream resolution |
| | `#player-error-switch-btn` | `<button class="btn btn-secondary">` | `data-nav="true" data-nav-group="player-error"` | Open server modal |
