## 6. Zero DOM Sink Remediation Specification

An audit of `app/js/player.js` revealed 6 instances of `.innerHTML =`:

| Occurrence | Line Numbers | Current Code Pattern | Security / Architectural Risk | Remediation DOM API |
|------------|--------------|----------------------|-------------------------------|---------------------|
| 1 | 1650, 1657 | `d.playIcon.innerHTML = '<rect.../>'` / `d.playIcon.innerHTML = '<polygon.../>'` | SVG HTML string parsing in playback loop | `clearElement` + `createSvgElement('rect' / 'polygon')` |
| 2 | 1693, 1695 | `d.feedbackIcon.innerHTML = '<polyline.../><path.../>'` | SVG string injection during rapid remote seek | `clearElement` + `createSvgElement('polyline', 'path')` |
| 3 | 1736 | `d.subsList.innerHTML = '';` | Dynamic container wipe via innerHTML | `clearElement(d.subsList)` |
| 4 | 1745–1747 | `item.innerHTML = '<span class="track-name">' + (track.label \|\| 'Track') + '</span>...'` | Unescaped string concatenation from manifest/track metadata | `document.createElement('span')` + `textContent` |
| 5 | 1782 | `d.serverList.innerHTML = '';` | Dynamic container wipe via innerHTML | `clearElement(d.serverList)` |
| 6 | 1796–1801 | `item.innerHTML = '<div class="server-item-left">...'` | Dynamic HTML string template for cluster servers | Structured `document.createElement` + `textContent` |

### 6.1 Pure DOM Helper Definitions for `app/js/player.js`
```javascript
/**
 * Safely removes all child nodes from an element (Zero DOM sink).
 * @param {HTMLElement|SVGElement} element
 */
function clearElement(element) {
  if (!element) return;
  while (element.firstChild) {
    element.removeChild(element.firstChild);
  }
}

/**
 * Creates an SVG element with given attributes (Zero DOM sink).
 * @param {string} tag
 * @param {Object} attrs
 * @returns {SVGElement}
 */
function createSvgElement(tag, attrs) {
  var el = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', tag);
  if (attrs) {
    for (var key in attrs) {
      if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(attrs, key)) {
        el.setAttribute(key, attrs[key]);
      }
    }
  }
  return el;
}
```

